@startuml supervision_failure

title Supervision Failure

box "Main loop thread" #F0F4FA
participant "ProcessGroupManager" as PGM
participant "Graph" as Graph
end box

box "Worker or Main Thread" #f0faf4
participant "IComponent" as Component
end box

queue "Component Event Queue" as EventQueue

box "Alive supervision thread" #FAF0F4
participant "Alive Supervision" as Supervision
participant "RecoveryClient" as Recovery
end box

participant "Supervised Process" as Process

note over Graph: graph is in state kSuccess:\nthe Run Target is active

' --- detection ---------------------------------------------------------------
activate Process
Process -> Supervision: alive indications
note right of Supervision
  Supervision was started for this process when the component
  was activated - see Component Activation.
end note

Supervision -> Supervision ++: check the supervision cycle

alt #F2FAF2 the indications arrive as configured
    note right of Supervision: nothing is reported, the next cycle is checked

else #Pink the configured tolerance is exceeded
    Supervision -> Recovery ++: request recovery for the component
    Recovery -> EventQueue: supervision failure of the component
    deactivate Recovery
    note right of Supervision
      The process identifier and the timestamp of the failure are
      reported. The supervision thread never touches the graph and
      never stops the process itself.
    end note
end
deactivate Supervision

' --- reaction ----------------------------------------------------------------
EventQueue -> PGM ++: component event
PGM -> Graph ++: apply the component event
Graph -> Component ++: notify the component of the supervision failure

alt #White the component is not ready
    note over Component
      The component is already deactivated, or currently being
      deactivated or re-activated: the failure is ignored.
    end note

else #White component was restarted after the failure timestamp
    note over Component
      The failure belongs to a previous run of the process:
      the failure is ignored.
    end note

else #White the process has already terminated
    note over Component
      The termination is already being reported through the
      OsHandler thread: the failure is ignored.
    end note

else #Pink the failure belongs to the running process
    Component -> Process: force termination (SIGKILL)
    destroy Process
end

deactivate Component
deactivate Graph
deactivate PGM

' --- recovery ----------------------------------------------------------------
note over PGM
  The killed process is detected by the OsHandler thread and reported
  as an unexpected termination. The graph leaves the active Run Target
  and the main loop starts a transition to the fallback Run Target -
  see Process Termination.
end note

legend bottom
  The reaction to a supervision failure is to kill the process. The recovery
  itself is the same as for any other unexpected process termination.
end legend

@enduml
